            {
                "entry_id": "16ef5291-55e0-3b13-885b-575941238598",
                "word": "agentique",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5996ae95-6970-480a-a7ab-7307d3991466",
                        "entry_id": "16ef5291-55e0-3b13-885b-575941238598",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "agentiques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0bf32718-3b0f-3ed3-8a59-8cf011abad6b",
                        "entry_id": "16ef5291-55e0-3b13-885b-575941238598",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif à un agent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3304fdb7-5334-30d2-9a17-f28cc44a4288",
                        "entry_id": "16ef5291-55e0-3b13-885b-575941238598",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif à l'état ou au comportement d'un individu qui agit en tant qu'agent exécutant les ordres d'une autorité, souvent sans questionner la moralité ou la légitimité de ces ordres."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ad7577a-01a1-4fe3-87e1-1cc939edcc26",
                                "sense_id": "3304fdb7-5334-30d2-9a17-f28cc44a4288",
                                "text": "L'autorité, pour Milgram, est un préalable indispensable à l'état agentique : un sujet ne perdra son état autonome que sous la pression d'une autorité qu'il considère comme légitime."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "06a3ed2b-93c1-34da-9f16-ecf01ffaa014",
                        "entry_id": "16ef5291-55e0-3b13-885b-575941238598",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif à un agent utilisant de l'intelligence artificielle générative."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Intelligence artificielle"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6aefc87d-bf39-4d34-9049-ae0c4d1d781b",
                                "sense_id": "06a3ed2b-93c1-34da-9f16-ecf01ffaa014",
                                "text": "Le capital sera utilisé pour acquérir les puissances de calcul et les données essentielles à la réalisation de percées dans le domaine des modèles agentiques."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "204a32c4-9618-40f9-b4cb-b297fcdc466e",
                                "sense_id": "06a3ed2b-93c1-34da-9f16-ecf01ffaa014",
                                "text": "L’IA agentique, plus ciblée que l’IA générative classique, gagne du terrain dans les entreprises, le cabinet d'études Forrester l'ayant désignée, en juin dernier, comme l'une des principales technologies émergentes pour 2025. Depuis, plusieurs organisations ont commencé à utiliser cette technologie, et de grands fournisseurs tels que Salesforce et ServiceNow proposent des agents d'IA à leurs clients."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6ef35aaf-6273-4596-bf19-cf28f760226d",
                        "source_entry_id": "16ef5291-55e0-3b13-885b-575941238598",
                        "source_sense_id": "3304fdb7-5334-30d2-9a17-f28cc44a4288",
                        "target_lang_word": "agentic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "agentic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bcb5bcb0-25d1-3405-8953-b7aa044db12e",
                                        "entry_id": "4f4d86b8-4fa1-3422-b9fe-324121537a69",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That behaves like an agent: able to express or expressing agency or control on one's own behalf or on the behalf of another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7801ca16-42c3-4506-8ebc-53f6331a4ac3",
                                                "sense_id": "bcb5bcb0-25d1-3405-8953-b7aa044db12e",
                                                "text": "From the perspective of the previous chapter, to change from a patient to an agent is to adopt or elaborate an agentic plot that the person lives (Howard 1989)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "875bdf40-0a1e-483f-b9a7-874af54a897c",
                                                "sense_id": "bcb5bcb0-25d1-3405-8953-b7aa044db12e",
                                                "text": "The next section examines ways in which network and partnership management may be able to reconcile self-organization with agentic intervention."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5447bff6-9bb9-4e34-abf8-4251246dd832",
                                                "sense_id": "bcb5bcb0-25d1-3405-8953-b7aa044db12e",
                                                "text": "Sometimes agentic systems detect and correct mistakes, but at other times, mistakes compound through multi-agent workflows and may give rise to computational cascades where errors, tool failures, or incomplete data can propagate undetected and enter the final output."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "53183ead-e34f-3bf2-aed8-d967cec8a103",
                                        "entry_id": "4f4d86b8-4fa1-3422-b9fe-324121537a69",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That obeys authority (introduced in Milgram's theory)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63f65a7a-933c-4ef6-abd5-9094ff4b6b2f",
                                                "sense_id": "53183ead-e34f-3bf2-aed8-d967cec8a103",
                                                "text": "Most individuals can be easily triggered to enter, and be comfortable in the agentic state."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd328c65-9db5-4a34-99c8-9eda0410eee9",
                                                "sense_id": "53183ead-e34f-3bf2-aed8-d967cec8a103",
                                                "text": "Milgram (1974) suggested that one factor contributing to the maintenance of obedience was that the individual in the obedience situation entered into an agentic state, which involves a person's giving up his or her normal moral and ethical standards in favor of those of the authority figure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8793bfb5-389e-3620-bec4-6b935320e19b",
                                        "entry_id": "4f4d86b8-4fa1-3422-b9fe-324121537a69",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having to do with performance, or achieving status."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be5184d6-d2d7-4d32-a8e3-07d2a9a62e54",
                                                "sense_id": "8793bfb5-389e-3620-bec4-6b935320e19b",
                                                "text": "If helping is a variation on the more general agentic theme of self-assertion and display, one might expect that power motivation would predict other forms of agentic striving in friendship experiences."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db601d62-2b96-3701-8abb-f58ba1b7ffa9",
                                        "entry_id": "4f4d86b8-4fa1-3422-b9fe-324121537a69",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having agency; able to make independent decisions in pursuit of a goal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35812327-b493-4bf1-9719-ef7c72456883",
                                                "sense_id": "db601d62-2b96-3701-8abb-f58ba1b7ffa9",
                                                "text": "Billy was agentic in his learning and didn't only do what the teacher told him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e810a60-6ec8-4272-a72c-3075dcce7612",
                                                "sense_id": "db601d62-2b96-3701-8abb-f58ba1b7ffa9",
                                                "text": "In agentic cognition the ego is a cognitive agent with tasks to accomplish."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7236935b-289f-4dcf-a8f8-a680c4f89a42",
                                                "sense_id": "db601d62-2b96-3701-8abb-f58ba1b7ffa9",
                                                "text": "Within this framework, with gender role self-perception conceptualized as independent of biological sex, the agentic construct includes characteristics such as goal-orientation, assertiveness, protectiveness, self-activation, and having the urge to master."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "302e33ae-5ab5-4be3-9578-84b9822c0850",
                                                "sense_id": "db601d62-2b96-3701-8abb-f58ba1b7ffa9",
                                                "text": "We have seen that the agentic self identifies values to be striven after, then makes decisions about which values/goals to pursue and then controls pursuit of those goals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f81fad7a-bcbb-4bc5-8501-00103c38cbd7",
                                                "sense_id": "db601d62-2b96-3701-8abb-f58ba1b7ffa9",
                                                "text": "A single, highly agentic AI system rapidly becomes superintelligent on all human tasks, in a world broadly similar to today. The objective function used to train the system (e.g. ‘maximise production’) doesn't push it to do what we really want, and the system's goals match the objective function."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ba7e404-60f3-4d5b-a57f-7833406cad5b",
                                                "sense_id": "db601d62-2b96-3701-8abb-f58ba1b7ffa9",
                                                "text": "While previous AI assistants were rules-based and had limited ability to act independently, agentic AI will be empowered to do more on our behalf."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
